Anouncing: Stars 0.9 (ELF-binary) for svgalib,
uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming

Remember those starfield screensavers ?
Stars does a bit more. Quite a lot more actually.

Basically it's just a toy with which you can move around a lot of
dots on your screen or fly through them. It has a lot of run-time options,
of which only some are currently documented, so just try it out.
It uses svgalib and currently only in 640x480x256 mode (svgalib doesn't
support my S3-964/TI3025 very well yet).

