Recently, I've received a few submissions for comp.os.linux.announce
in such a way that I assume they have arrived from mailing lists.
(When someone posts to this group, the news server automatically mails
the article to me, I check it out, and then put it into the group for
real.)

Please do not put linux-announce@news.ornl.gov on any mailing lists.
Always either post via news, or send it via mail by placing the address
in the To: or Cc: field.  (Otherwise you won't even get the automatic
response that your article arrived safely to my machine.)

Reason: I don't want to have my moderator mailbox start getting stuff
that wasn't meant to be sent to the newsgroup.  This happens much too
easily with a mailing list, even if you currently only intend to use
it for announcements that should go to the newsgroup as well.  Trust me
on this one. :-)

Thank you.

Lars Wirzenius, moderator, comp.os.linux.announce.

