If you have a personal web page on your ISP's server, you might need this
program:

You keep a local copy of a bunch of HTML files and stuff, which are
supposed to also be stored at your ISP's web server. Every time you update a
local file, you must remember to copy that file to your ISP's server.

This program automates that task by recording a time stamp for each file in
your HTML directory, and when you run it, any files which are newer than the
corresponding time stamps are copied to the server via FTP, and the time stamp
is updated.  Any subdirectories are automatically descended into.

