  Time:   11:00 to 15:00 (Doors open at 10:00)
  Place:  The Rivenhall Village Hall (near Witham)
  Cost:   Maximum GBP 1 per person to cover hall hire costs

About 16 people have already confirmed they are coming.  With the people
who may be coming, but cannot yet say for sure, numbers could rise to
24.  An ascii map with directions to the meeting is available by e-mail 
on request.  

Peter Onion will talk of his experiences with the latest Linux kernels
and we will plan for whatever people want from the group in future.  The 
approximate agenda is included below.  

A few people will be bringing their Linux boxes, so there will be things
to play with.  I know of four boxes that are currently due to arrive.  
There will be an Ethernet hub to which people can attach (BNC, RJ45 and 
I've even got some AUI transceivers too).

I believe tea, coffee and biscuits will be available during the day at
about 50p a go, and lunch will either be bring-your-own or in the local
pub (probably the Rivenhall Fox).


                  Approximate Agenda for 29/6/96
                  ==============================

  10:00    Start-up.  Setting up and playing with the computers.

  11:15    Introductory discussion relating to the aims and operation of
           the user group.  What do people want to get from the group?
           What are people interested in doing with/for/in the group?

  12:00    Peter Onion's presentation - experiences of the latest Linux 
           kernels and life at the leading edge.

  12:45    Lunch.  We will probably follow (by car) one of the locals to
           the nearest pub.

