Hi :)

I'm happy to announce that Pixcon/Anitroll release 1.0 is finally
available to the public.

What is Pixcon & Anitroll you may ask?  Pixcon & Anitroll is a 3D
rendering and animation package available for FREE.  Did I say FREE?
Yes I did.  Not only is it FREE, but I've also included the source code.

Pixcon is a 3D renderer that creates high quality images by using a
combination of 11 rendering primitives.  Anitroll is a forward kinematic
hierarchical based animation system that has some support for some
non-kinematic based animation (such as flock of birds, and autonomous
cameras).  These tools are based upon the Graph library which is full
of those neat rendering and animation algorithms that those 3D FAQs
keep mentioning...

Why Pixcon & Anitroll?  Well, renderers like Alias, Renderman, Wavefront, 3DS,
Softimage, etc are too expensive for average users, and require expensive
hardware.  Conventional freeware renders like BMRT, Rayshade, and POV are
slow (they're raytracers...).  Pixcon & Anitroll is FREE, and doesn't take
a long time to render (true, its not real time... but I'm working on it).
It also implements some rendering techniques that have yet to be published
(or will be in SIGGRAPH '96 - if the paper gets published).

If you aren't convinced yet, I invite you to look at the Pixcon & Anitroll
Home page at:

		http://www.sites.com/~pixcon

where I have a gallery that shows off some of the capabilities of Pixcon.

And if you like it, you can download the source from the same URL.

	* Available for PC-Linux systems and SGI-IRIX 5.2/5.3/6.02 *

BTW, If you have any comments email me at aharper@acetef.nawcad.navy.mil
or dunbar@saltmine.radix.net.

