totem version 2.0.1 now available!


What It Is
==========

Totem is a small kernel driver module which implements a proc filesystem
file /proc/totem.  This file provides the symbolic totem, or animal,
associated with your kernel release.  Sample totem values would include:

Kernel          Totem
- ----------      ---------------------------------------------
1.3.85          Greased HedgeHog handing out Jolt Cola
pre2.0.4        Impatient HedgeHog on Quaaludes
pre2.0.13       Impatient HedgeHog on Garlic Ice Cream
2.0.0           Zen Penguin on Endorphins
2.1.98          Stealth Penguin selling Vitamins
- ----------      ---------------------------------------------

What It's Good For
==================

Impressing your friends with your high degree of cool.  Confusing
non-Linux-users with obscure references to strange animals.  Learning a
little about how to write a kernel driver module that uses the proc
filesystem, from a small, well-documented model.  :)

The License
===========

Totem is GPL'ed.  You wouldn't have it any other way, would you? :)

Thanks To:
=========

Andrew Esh for the idea, Joel Mazsak for the initial implementation from
which I stole ruthlessly.  :) Bjorn Ekwall for the current modules package. 
Allesandro Rubini for the sample code.  The new, self-rejuvenating Kernel
Hacker's guide on http://www.redhat.com:8080/HyperNews/get/khg.html.  Johann
Myrene and company for the miscellaneous device driver code which helped me
sort some things out.

And Linus Benedict Torvalds, without whom none of this would have been
necessary, or even desirable.  :)


:) lilo



