To commemorate the release of version 2.0 of the Linux kernel, the latest
version of the ax25-utils, aptly named ax25-utils-2.0 have been released. 
These utilities are essential if you intend to use the kernel based AX.25
and NET/ROM amateur radio protocols in any form. The utilities range from
the program needed to start an AX.25 interface to a BPQ-like node front
end and almost everything else between. 

If you use any form of amateur radio software under Linux, may I 
recommend that you subscribe to the linux-hams mailing list. This may be 
achieved by sending a message to Majordomo@vger.rutgers.edu with the 
following in the body of the message:

subscribe linux-hams
end

That way you can be sure of keeping up with latest news and patches that
are associated with amateur radio use of Linux, as well as the occasional 
flame war to keep everyone entertained.

May I also recommend that you download a copy of the AX25-HOWTO and the 
HAM-HOWTO from any standard Linux mirror site, they will be found with 
the other HOWTO documents. The former deals specifically with configuring 
the kernel based AX.25 and NET/ROM code (using these utilities) and 
should be read thoroughly before asking for help. The latter deals with 
more general Linux amateur radio usage.

The LSM entry for the utilities is below:

