Addison Wesley Longman has just published our book:

	Beck, Boehme, Dziadzka, Kunitz, Magnus, Verworner
	"Linux Kernel Internals"
	Addison Wesley Longman 1996
	ISBN: 0-201-87741-4

This is a  translation of the German book: "Linux Kernel
Programmierung", 3. edition. 

Based on Linux 1.2 the book covers

    * important data structures and algorithms
    * memory management
    * interprocess communication
    * file systems
    * device drivers
    * network implementation
    * kernel modules
    * debugging
    * an overview about all system calls
    * the proc file system
    * the boot process.

So we think there is enough interesting stuff to read. 

You might ask: Why isn't the book about 2.0? Sorry, that is
impossible. You can't make a book over night. We are working on
it, promised.

