	4Front Technologies announces UNIX Sound System for Linux

LOS ANGELES: 4Front Technologies is pleased to announce the 
availability of UNIX Sound System(TM) for Linux 2.0.0.

USS/Linux provides device drivers for a wide variety of sound cards and
audio hardware for Linux. USS/Linux is a set of dynamically loadable
kernel modules that allow Linux users to add digital audio and MIDI
music capabilities to their Linux workstations without having to
recompile the Linux kernel with the freeware sound drivers (USS/Lite).
Additionally, USS/Linux is FULLY supported as a commercial Linux
product.

USS/Linux comes with a curses based configuration program which enables
users to easily identify and configure their audio hardware. The
program detects hardware configuration conflicts and allows the user
the make necessary changes. USS/Linux has a database of over 100 brand 
name sound cards with their factory settings and possible configuration 
values. Users can change settings on the fly without having to
recompile the kernel. USS/Linux also supports several PnP soundcards
for which there is no support in the freeware Linux sound drivers.

4Front Technologies has developed USS/Linux to be compatible with
USS/Lite for base audio functionality. There are additional audio
interfaces provided for extended functionality.


Functionally, USS provides support for:
- ---------------------------------------
o 8bit and 16bit stereo digital audio playback and sampling
o FM sound synthesis
o Wavetable MIDI synthesis
o MIDI input and output
o Audio Mixer for setting input and output levels

USS represents a major step in the unification of digital audio APIs
for UNIX. Currently, each UNIX vendor provides their own proprietary
audio API, making it difficult to write cross-platform audio
applications. With USS, developers can design their software on any
UNIX platform and be assured that it will be able to compile and run
without modification on any other UNIX variant supported by USS.

The retail price for USS/Linux is $30.00. Visitors to 4Front's Web site
at http://www.4front-tech.com/linux.html can download a free version of
USS/Linux and test-drive it until July 31, 1996. After the trial period
the drivers will cease to be functional.

