		          PENTIUM FTPOV/POVRay 2.2
                                   RELEASE

I have compiled an i586/P5 optimizied version of POVRay 2.2, and later 
adapted the FTPOV (Faster Then POVRay) patches to the distribution.  It 
was mainly for my own use, but because some people became interested, I 
am making this announcement. 

The software was compiled with gcc-2.7.2p-pl8, from the Pentium Compiler 
Group.  The Faster Than POVRay patches were adapted to UNIX (they were 
made for DOS), and included, along with X11 output support.  

There are some bugs.  The option pager is broken, and certain scenes will 
refuse to render out, resulting in a segmentation fault or a floating point 
exception.  If this happens it is recommended that you adjust some of the 
'unofficial' options such as vista buffering.  No more changes will be 
made to this, as I am waiting to do similar for POVRay 3.0.

This hack of POVRay will render a scene 15-20% faster on average, but I 
have seen improvements of up to 25%.

Running this binary on a 386/486 system will result in renders that are 
at least 10% faster, so you might want to check this out even if you do 
not have a i586/P5 CPU. 

The binary is provided on the Pentium Compiler Groups Pentium 
Applications Page, accessible at:

http://www-iss.mach.uni-karlsruhe.de/pcg/applic.html   [EUROPE]
http://goof.com/pcg/applic.html                        [USA]
http://nightflight.com/~pcg/applic.html                [USA]
http://linux.cis.nctu.edu.tw/pcg/applic.html           [TAIWAN]

This version is unsupported and you are using it at your own risk.  You 
must also pick up the standard POVRay distribution, because all that is 
provided at the sites above is (using Netscrape binary terminology) the 
gzipped i586-unknown-linux-elf binary.
 
Have fun...

If you have any questions, you can e-mail me at trn@gate.net, or contact 
me on IRC with the nickname TrN in #Linux on SFnet (irc.gate.net) or DALNet 
(irc.dal.net).  Remember, this is unsupported software, and I did this 
out of the kindness of my heart.  I will, however, try to help you out 
with your problems.  

