-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

I have released a minor update to my BusLogic driver which includes the
following changes:

o The preferred Tagged Queue Depth has been reduced from 31 to 28.  Larger
  Tagged Queue Depths can still be selected with command line arguments.

o The code has been reorganized slightly and data structure definitions have
  been changed in minor ways for compatibility with non-Intel architecture
  machines.

Though this driver version was already released with Linux 2.0, it was only a
couple of days ago that I had the opportunity to verify that a BT-948 works
correctly with Linux running on the Alpha AXP architecture.  All recent PCI and
EISA BusLogic host adapters should now be compatible with Alpha AXP systems.

Versions 1.2.4 and 2.0.4 of my BusLogic driver are now available for FTP from:

    ftp://ftp.dandelion.com/BusLogic-1.2.4.tar.gz
    ftp://ftp.dandelion.com/BusLogic-2.0.4.tar.gz

In addition, since the changes are so minor and some people have heavily
patched Linux 1.2.13 source trees, I've also made a patch available that will
upgrade from version 1.2.3 of the driver directly to 1.2.4:

    ftp://ftp.dandelion.com/BusLogic-1.2.4.upgrade.gz

If you have Linux 2.0 or above, then BusLogic 2.0.4 is already included.  In
all likelihood, this will be the last release of my BusLogic driver for 1.2.13.

		Leonard


