their answers to questions that they get.  We think that this
will provide a win-win situation for everyone:

 o Linux users get common questions answered.
 o Linux support staff don't have to deal with the same questions
   over and over any more.
 * Linux support staff get publicity with each answer.
 * Linux users can place fairly high trust in the answers,
   because a bad answer would be bad publicity for the
   tech support staff giving the answer.

I could go on, but you get the idea.

Where necessary, names, IP numbers, passwords, and so on should
(and will) be changed to protect the guilty--er--innocent.

All commercial support staffs *AND* volunteer Linux supporters on
usenet, irc, and other forums are encouraged to participate.  For
more information, please send mail to linux@ssc.com (or simply
reply to this post) and express your interest in "Best of tech
support".  You will be contacted with instructions including
deadlines for question and answer submission.

