- --------------------------------------------------------------
- -==== FETCHPOP1.6BETA with sendmail and procmail support ====-

This is fetchpop1.6 beta version. 
If you want stable and well-tested version, get 1.4.

I added a few more options in 1.6 to support procmail and sendmail.
The new option flags are -o, -p, and -s.
 
 -o is used to specify user mail folder. without -o ( -s or  -p ), 
    the retrieved mails go to $MAIL folder.
 -s uses sendmail as a delivery agent, instead of 
    directly writing retrieved mails to a file. NOT RECOMMENDED.
 -p uses procmail/formail as a delivery and mail formating tool. 
    HIGHLY RECOMMENDED!!!.  

YOU DO NOT NEED SENDMAIL OR PROCMAIL TO USE FETCHPOP. These are extra
features.

Using procmail/formail package is better way to use as mail delivery
than
using sendmail. Using sendmail for mail delivery with fetchpop has
limitation,
such as the sender of mails you retrieved becomes you, not the person
who sent 
the mail to remote mail server. Using formail does not have this
limitation 
,so that mail filtering is done nicely. 
Even though you do not do mail filtering, get procmail and install it.
procmail 
should be suid as mentioned in the file INSTALL in procmail. 
procmail can be obtained from
  ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/Mail/mailhandlers/procmail-3.XX.tar.gz
  ftp://ftp.net.ohio-state.edu/pub/networking/mail/procmail
  ftp://ftp.psg.com/pub/unix/procmail

If you prefer well-tested direct writing to mail folder file,
you do not need to have procmail.

For more information about usage of fetchpop and other options, 
please refer to fetchpop man page. 
( If you installed fetchpop, do 'man fetchpop' or
do 'nroff -man fetchpop.1L | more )

